So there are 2 conditions that BOTH must be activated to initiate the BSPD circuit: The brake pressure must exceed the set threshold value(its usually 30 bar so less than or equal to 30), and also either 1. The power delivered to motors is more than or equal to 5kW or 2. the throttle position is more than 25% over the idle position.

Now once this happens, there will be analog signals(idk if this should be more specific but for now at the most basic level an analog signal is sent) that each go to an Operational Amplifier that is in a comparator circuit. Both of the analog signals will flow into the inverting input, while there is a threshold comparing voltage going into the non-inverting input(with some resistors that I assume is to cut down the voltage ???? I need to research more so I can fully understand full picture). If the voltage in the inverting input is greater than non-inverting one, output is high(1) and voltage will flow. If the opposite happens, the output is low(0) and I think it goes to ground???(I will edit this when I find the definite answer). Since both of these conditions need to be true, we can use an AND gate so that there is an output of 1(high) when both are true.

